  "manual_observations": [
    "Original Chinese quantization explanation correctly describes reducing numeric precision; QAT32 instead describes storing state/checkpointing. Both stop at the32-token cap, but the semantic difference precedes the cap.",
    "Original answers only Beijing and EOS to the city-only instruction. QAT32 continues with extra unsupported prose. This is a matched development-prompt instruction regression.",
    "Both correctly answer the two arithmetic probes, exactOK and the short translation. Five tiny exact probes pass in original versus four in QAT32; this is not a model-accuracy or retention score.",
    "All three original conceptual explanations also reach the32-token cap. Truncation by itself cannot be attributed to quantization.",
    "These results support testing broader bilingual instruction-context distillation after only4096 English training tokens. They do not prove data coverage is the sole cause, exclude implementation defects, or establish how much more training is sufficient.",
    "The same development prompts informed the next experiment. Future capability acceptance needs separate unseen evaluation."
  ],
